        "id": 122931,
        "name": "The Burning Stickman",
        "username": "The_Burning_Stickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_burning_stickman/{size}/2003_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-04-11T15:34:58.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>As a group, we tend to pick the villain well beforehand, almost always opting for someone we haven't faced before (unless we lost to a given villain before, in which case we go for revenge), and we try to pick an environment that fits with the villain in question or the scenario we've got in mind.</p><p>Being that I know the game the best of the people I play with, I will usually make recommendations for heroes based on what we need and the level of complexity, then I'll pick my character to fill any holes we have in the group. Or, if the villain's simple enough and I think we have the bases covered, I try someone I haven't played with much.</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:56:44.914Z",
